WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.789
"Go, Luke!" cheered Katie.

2
00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.692
She was waving the ribbon wand she had just made.

3
00:00:19.693 --> 00:00:23.028
Luke was stomping across the room on stilts.

4
00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:25.943
He was practicing for the parade.

5
00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:30.596
"Left, right, left, right!" directed Mrs. Penkov.

6
00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:34.247
"Be careful!" called AJ.

7
00:00:34.248 --> 00:00:40.669
Campers beat on their drums, shook their shakers, and twirled their twirlers.

8
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.997
Today was day five of camp.

9
00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:50.815
Saturday was Willow Creek's birthday, and the campers were almost ready for the parade.

10
00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:54.524
But time was running out for the scavenger hunt.

11
00:00:54.525 --> 00:01:01.010
In less than two days, they had to turn in their bags—ready or not.

12
00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:06.334
That afternoon the Earthworms gathered at Fried Pie Heaven.

13
00:01:06.335 --> 00:01:09.343
Katie took a bite of peach fried pie.

14
00:01:09.344 --> 00:01:14.199
"Luke's getting his hair cut," she said. "He'll be late."

15
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.421
"You're not supposed to talk with food in your mouth," said AJ.

16
00:01:19.422 --> 00:01:21.272
Katie took another bite.

17
00:01:21.273 --> 00:01:26.577
"I'll remember that next time," she said with her mouth full.

18
00:01:26.578 --> 00:01:31.144
Emily was checking the scavenger hunt list one more time.

19
00:01:31.145 --> 00:01:35.975
"We're lucky my dad had that old campaign button," she said.

20
00:01:35.976 --> 00:01:39.969
"Now the only thing we're missing is—"

21
00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:43.822
Just then Luke ran into the coffee shop.

22
00:01:43.823 --> 00:01:47.295
"Guess what I learned at the barber shop!" he said.

23
00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:50.065
Luke sat down at the table.

24
00:01:50.066 --> 00:01:57.074
"No one in Willow Creek is allowed to own a dog that barks too loud or too often!"

25
00:01:57.075 --> 00:02:00.052
"So?" said AJ.

26
00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:03.539
"So it's a law!" said Luke.

27
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:05.472
"A Willow Creek law!"

28
00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:09.716
said Emily, waving the scavenger list in the air.

29
00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:12.712
"Do you know what this means, team?"

30
00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:18.070
"We're almost finished with the hunt!" said Katie.

31
00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:23.672
Down the street at the library, the Tornadoes were checking their list too.

32
00:02:23.673 --> 00:02:27.768
"Where's the note from Mr. Potter?" asked Laura.

33
00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:30.393
"It's right here," said Carlos.

34
00:02:30.394 --> 00:02:32.393
"Milton Christopher Potter.

35
00:02:32.394 --> 00:02:35.460
Ninety-seven years old."

36
00:02:35.461 --> 00:02:38.431
Now everyone turned to Manny.

37
00:02:38.432 --> 00:02:42.585
"Manny," said Joy with her grown-up voice.

38
00:02:42.586 --> 00:02:46.410
"We are depending on your outstanding counting skills.

39
00:02:46.411 --> 00:02:49.244
Are you ready to report?"

40
00:02:49.245 --> 00:02:52.895
"Yes, I am," said Manny.

41
00:02:52.896 --> 00:02:54.775
"Okay," said Joy.

42
00:02:54.776 --> 00:02:59.351
"How many stop signs did you count on Main Street?"

43
00:02:59.352 --> 00:03:02.662
"Seven," said Manny.

44
00:03:02.663 --> 00:03:04.732
"Mailboxes?"

45
00:03:04.733 --> 00:03:06.298
"Two."

46
00:03:06.299 --> 00:03:10.923
"And last how many streetlamps did you count?"

47
00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.224
"Eighteen."

48
00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:15.708
Laura looked up from the list.

49
00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:18.095
"We're done with the hunt!"

50
00:03:18.096 --> 00:03:22.963
"Hooray!" cheered the Tornadoes.

51
00:03:22.964 --> 00:03:29.412
"Shh!" said Mrs. Donovan. "Use your library voices, please!"

52
00:03:29.413 --> 00:03:33.735
"We're going to win!" whispered Joy.

53
00:03:33.736 --> 00:03:36.919
Friday was the last day of camp.

54
00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:39.402
"Teams!" said Mrs. Penkov.

55
00:03:39.403 --> 00:03:42.208
"Are you ready to turn in your bags?"

56
00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:46.256
"The Earthworms are ready!" called AJ.

57
00:03:46.257 --> 00:03:51.465
He grabbed the team bag and carried it up to Mrs. Penkov.

58
00:03:51.466 --> 00:03:56.449
"It's the marble lady!" squeaked Manny as AJ passed by.

59
00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:59.392
The Earthworms' jaws dropped.

60
00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:04.456
"What? That was YOU?" sputtered Katie.

61
00:04:04.457 --> 00:04:06.202
She shook her fist.

62
00:04:06.203 --> 00:04:10.926
The Tornadoes burst out laughing.

63
00:04:10.927 --> 00:04:15.076
The other teams carried their bags to Mrs. Penkov.

64
00:04:15.077 --> 00:04:24.335
She arranged them in a row on the table: Airplanes, Lizards, Watermelons, Earthworms, Tornadoes.

65
00:04:24.336 --> 00:04:28.020
"When will you announce the winner?" asked Joy.

66
00:04:28.021 --> 00:04:32.017
"After the parade," said Mrs. Penkov.

67
00:04:32.018 --> 00:04:37.032
"And then you'll give out the prizes, right?" said Katie.

68
00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:39.908
"Of course," said Mrs. Penkov.

69
00:04:39.909 --> 00:04:44.929
"And since you have worked so hard, I think you all deserve a prize."

70
00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.010
She pulled a big box from under the table.

71
00:04:48.011 --> 00:04:55.578
"Surprise!" she cried. "HAPPY BIRTHDAY WILLOW CREEK T-shirts!"

72
00:04:55.579 --> 00:05:00.130
The day campers clapped and cheered.

73
00:05:00.131 --> 00:05:02.568
"T-shirts for everyone!"

74
00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:07.260
Mrs. Penkov laughed and tossed T-shirts right and left.

75
00:05:07.261 --> 00:05:09.053
"Yellow for the Airplanes.

76
00:05:09.054 --> 00:05:10.980
Blue for the Tornadoes.

77
00:05:10.981 --> 00:05:13.321
Green for the Lizards.

78
00:05:13.322 --> 00:05:15.121
Red for the Watermelons.

79
00:05:15.122 --> 00:05:18.338
And orange for the Earthworms."

80
00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:23.268
"Thank you, Mrs. Penkov!" shouted the campers.

81
00:05:23.269 --> 00:05:26.157
"You're welcome," said Mrs. Penkov.

82
00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.647
"But—we still have work to do!

83
00:05:28.648 --> 00:05:31.958
The marchers can help me finish our banner.

84
00:05:31.959 --> 00:05:35.106
The riders can decorate their bikes.

85
00:05:35.107 --> 00:05:38.436
And Luke, get up on those stilts and practice!

86
00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:42.796
Tomorrow is the big day!"
